            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Everything works as expected:\r\n\r\n- There is no special icons for '.git' or '.github' directories because file explorer plugin in the screenshot (probably, 'neo-tree.nvim' or 'nvim-tree.lua') does not have direct support for 'mini.icons'. Instead it probably uses mocked 'nvim-web-devicons' which does not have support for special directory icons. You can verify that everything works as expected by executing the following command `:=MiniIcons.get('directory', '.git')` or by using 'mini.files'.\r\n- The exclamation mark for 'yml' is how its intended icon looks. You can navigate to https://www.nerdfonts.com/cheat-sheet and search for \"yml\". If you don't like this particular glyph, you can customize it [following example from help page](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/cf81e70e8f1fdc36a3c684efc45c4ee561285137/doc/mini-icons.txt#L235-L248).",
